1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"page-hero","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell article-header","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow light","children":"Tajweed"}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"How to Learn Quran with Tajweed Online, Step by Step"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"page-hero-copy","children":"Learn what an online Tajweed course should cover and how live correction can improve recitation over time."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-meta","children":[["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-08-28","children":["Published ","August 28, 2026"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"7 min read"}]]}]]}]}],["$","$Ld",null,{"items":[{"name":"Home","href":"/"},{"name":"Blog","href":"/blog/"},{"name":"How to Learn Quran with Tajweed Online, Step by Step"}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"section section-paper","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell article-body","children":[[["$","section","Tajweed is learned through listening and practice",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Tajweed is learned through listening and practice"}],[["$","p","Reading about Tajweed rules is useful, but correct application also requires listening, demonstration and repeated practice. In a live online lesson, the tutor can hear a learner's pronunciation and identify patterns that may be difficult to notice alone.",{"children":"Reading about Tajweed rules is useful, but correct application also requires listening, demonstration and repeated practice. In a live online lesson, the tutor can hear a learner's pronunciation and identify patterns that may be difficult to notice alone."}],["$","p","A structured course normally begins from the learner's present reading ability. Some learners need work on individual letter sounds before moving to longer recitation, while others can begin by applying rules within selected passages.",{"children":"A structured course normally begins from the learner's present reading ability. Some learners need work on individual letter sounds before moving to longer recitation, while others can begin by applying rules within selected passages."}]]]}],["$","section","Build one skill at a time",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Build one skill at a time"}],[["$","p","Trying to correct every rule in one lesson can feel overwhelming. A clearer approach is to focus on a small number of articulation or recitation points, practise them carefully and revisit them in later lessons.",{"children":"Trying to correct every rule in one lesson can feel overwhelming. A clearer approach is to focus on a small number of articulation or recitation points, practise them carefully and revisit them in later lessons."}],["$","p","Recording personal correction notes can help. Instead of copying a long rule list, write down the exact letters, words or reading habits that need attention and practise those before the next session.",{"children":"Recording personal correction notes can help. Instead of copying a long rule list, write down the exact letters, words or reading habits that need attention and practise those before the next session."}]]]}],["$","section","Choose consistency over speed",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Choose consistency over speed"}],[["$","p","Careful recitation develops through regular correction. Short, frequent practice is often easier to maintain than occasional long sessions. Learners should ask questions, repeat difficult sounds and allow enough time for accurate habits to become natural.",{"children":"Careful recitation develops through regular correction. Short, frequent practice is often easier to maintain than occasional long sessions. Learners should ask questions, repeat difficult sounds and allow enough time for accurate habits to become natural."}],"$Le"]]}]],"$Lf"]}]}],"$L10","$L11"]}]
